+## D9 — Close the cyclic crossing-wall ambiguity and harden scalar inputs
+
+**Reproduced defect.** In the version-3.0 schedule, easy indices `0..3` could show vertical-unequal, vertical-equal, and horizontal-three demonstrations followed by a 2×2 crossing-wall query. An independently written `single_axis_only` rival matched all three labels but left the query unchanged; the full cyclic probe found 18 such ambiguities among 96 rotations.
+
+**Decision.** Declare `single_axis_only` as a semantic rival and lesson competitor, but not as a canonical shortcut because canonical 2×2 examples already refute it. Replace the eight-profile cycle with a 12-profile `GGNN` topology cadence, preserve alternating distinct/reused color patterns, cover all eight layout/scale combinations, and use difficulty phase offsets `0/1/2`. Make `lesson_identifiable` query-aware so a surviving rival is an ambiguity only when it changes the query answer. Add exact integer/nonnegative checks for `seed` and `sample_index`.
+
+**Why.** In any four consecutive samples, exactly two are crossing-wall grids and exactly two use reused colors. Rotating either witness into the query leaves another witness among the demonstrations, so both declared rivals are refuted without changing the authority or expanding the legal grammar. Strict scalar checks prevent coercion-like values from silently changing deterministic identities.
+
+**Alternatives rejected.** A simple `vertical, horizontal, grid` repetition still permits four-sample windows with exactly one grid, so it fails under arbitrary query rotation. Making the rival query-aware without changing the schedule would correctly describe ambiguity but would not teach the missing topology. Expanding the domain beyond reviewed full-wall rectangles was unnecessary.
+
+**Evidence.** The independent pre-repair probe failed with 18/96 ambiguous rotations and the focused regression failed first. The post-repair probe passes 144/144 rotations; the task suite passes 112 tests; the compact curriculum probe covers 384 generated default inputs, all 64 exact override/band combinations, and independent parity for both rivals. Six representative inputs were executed by the pinned Racket authority (`5f0096488100`), with 6/6 oracle matches and four clear query rotations.
+
+**Remaining limitation.** The `GGNN` schedule gives 2×2 layouts half of default samples to guarantee cyclic identifiability. This is a deliberate teaching bias, not a claim that the canonical distribution is 50% crossing-wall grids.
